          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cèsuǒ is built from cè 'a privy' and suǒ 'a place', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tsrhiH and srjoX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The modern cè is not the regular outcome of that form, and how it came is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
